PREREQUISITES:
- directories yields/catalogs and yields/runs
- catalogs with right naming format imported by date in yields/catalogs
(right naming format is three '_' and then either SAG13_baseline/optimistic/pessimistic, Dressing2015_baseline/optimistic/pessimistic, or Bryson2021_hab2high/low)
- virtual environment with right version of lifesim (python 3.12 works)

AUTOMATION:
- activate virtual environment
- run either lifesim-yieldanalysis or lifesim-yieldanalysis init, this will create a config file in the current working directory
- adjust the config file
- run lifesim-yieldanalysis config_file.py
- wait :)

COMMANDS: 
- lifesim-yieldanalysis or lifesim-yieldanalysis init: creates yield_config template
- lifesim-yieldanalysis lifesim_config: creates lifesim config template
- lifesim-yieldanalysis catalog_merge: creates catalog_merge csv template
- lifesim-yieldanalysis optimizer_scenarios: creates optimizer_scenarios csv template
- lifesim-yieldanalysis yield_config.py: runs the yield calculation

WHAT THE AUTOMATION DOES:
- creates all necessary files to go through the entire yields process
- creates directories per catalog and calculates the snr_1h, merges data from the catalogs, optimises mission time
- sends everything to the euler queue, with dependencies

NOTES:
- catalogs are split after the third '_' for easier readability, adjust if naming convention of catalogs is changed, also adjust the optimizer csvs